    <dashboard _.fcp.AccessibleZoneTabOrder.true...enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Payment Report Guide'>
      <repository-location derived-from='http://ip-172-31-0-143:8041/t/Talabat/workbooks/RiderPaymentReport/PaymentReportGuide?rev=' id='PaymentReportGuide' path='/t/Talabat/workbooks/RiderPaymentReport' revision='' site='Talabat' />
      <style />
      <size maxheight='1300' maxwidth='1600' minheight='1300' minwidth='1600' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='88734' id='43' param='horz' type-v2='layout-flow' w='99000' x='500' y='10651'>
            <zone h='88734' id='69' name='descriptions' show-title='false' w='72125' x='500' y='10651'>
              <layout-cache fixed-size-h='1141' fixed-size-w='1146' type-h='fixed' type-w='fixed' />
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='4' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
            <zone forceUpdate='true' h='88734' id='74' type-v2='text' w='26875' x='72625' y='10651'>
              <formatted-text>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Data Check</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>The following filters can be utilized to check for any discrepency in the payment records or invistigate any delivery status mismatch.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Mismatch status 1: </run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Talabat Deliveries that are completed in Hurrier but Failed in BOA. The user has the ability to filter out or include BOA failed payments in the report by Include Failed Order Payment Categories filter.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Mismatch status 2: </run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Talabat Deliveries that are cancelled in Hurrier but Successful in BOA. As Rooster is generating payment records as per Hurrier status, no payments will be available for these deliveries.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Multiple contracts paid flag: </run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>One delivery corresponding to multiple contracts. </run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Unpaid flag: </run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Completed deliveries that have no corresponding payment records. </run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Usually, these deliveries indicate misconfigured rules that are not covering some riders, contracts, vehicles, or job types. Rooster payment controls should be checked and the rules that should have been applied should be verified. Any of the following issues can be the cause</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>1- The rule timeframe doesnt cover the delivery (the rules can&apos;t be applied retroactively)</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>2- The rule doesn&apos;t apply to the riders&apos; specific contract, job type, vehicle, starting point etc.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>3- The rule filters are misspelled (the rules are case sensitive)</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>4- The rider level configrations are misspelled (the rules are case sensitive)</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>3PL Unpaid flag</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>: Completed deliveries that have no corresponding hidden payment records. </run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>Usually, these deliveries indicate misconfigured rules that are not covering some riders, contracts, vehicles, or job types.  The same checks above should be conducted.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>This usually indicates an issue with the data pipeline. In case any records were found, please reach out to the data team for invistigation.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>payment_record_count: </run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>On delivery level, how many payment records were considered. </run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>This can be used to detect overpaid deliveries. This can be indictive of a an issue in the data pipeline or duplicated rules. Please verify that no duplicated rules or rules that apply to the same set of deliveries exist on Rooster before raising this to the data team.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>If any discrepencies were found using the above control, the adjustment should be done manually after rectifying the issue.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              </formatted-text>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='4' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone h='10036' id='44' param='horz' type-v2='layout-flow' w='99000' x='500' y='615'>
            <zone h='10036' id='42' is-scaled='1' param='Image/Talabat_New_Brand_Logo-Colour_(3).png' type-v2='bitmap' w='6125' x='500' y='615'>
              <zone-style>
